"Where uploaded media files are stored. Cloud drivers require API "
"credentials."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:360
msgid "Signed URL Expiry (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:366
msgid ""
"How long signed URLs remain valid for private media files. Default: 3600 (1 "
"hour)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:403
msgid "View Event Retention (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:410
#. translators: %d: maximum allowed retention in days.
msgid ""
"How long raw view events are kept in the database. Aggregated counts (Total "
"Views, etc.) are NOT affected. Default: 90 days. Set to 0 to retain "
"forever. Maximum: %d."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:438
msgid "Compress uploaded images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:444
msgid ""
"Re-save each uploaded image with stronger compression to save space. Works "
"on JPEG, PNG, and GIF, and typically makes uploads 10 to 30 percent "
"smaller. For JPEG this is a lossy re-encode (about quality 92), so it is "
"off by default to keep your originals untouched - turn it on if storage "
"matters more than pixel-perfect originals. Removing hidden GPS/camera data "
"is a separate, lossless step controlled by Strip EXIF Data under General - "
"it does not depend on this setting. If you use EWWW, Imagify, Smush, or "
"ShortPixel, leave this off and let them handle it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:462
msgid "Create WebP copies for faster loading"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:468
msgid ""
"Save a second copy of every image in WebP format. WebP files are about 25 "
"to 35 percent smaller than JPEG, so pages load faster for your visitors. "
"Browsers that support WebP use the smaller file; older browsers keep using "
"the original. Already have older uploads to optimize? Visit a media item "
"and use Re-optimize, or ask your developer to run the bulk optimizer "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:488
msgid "Create AVIF copies for the smallest possible files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:502
#. translators: %s: a sentence stating whether this server can encode AVIF.
msgid ""
"Save a third copy of every image in the newer AVIF format. AVIF is around "
"30 to 50 percent smaller than WebP, so pages load even faster on modern "
"browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari 16.4+, Edge). Older browsers fall back to "
"WebP, then the original. Encoding AVIF is much slower than WebP so uploads "
"will take longer. %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:504
msgid "This server can encode AVIF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:505
msgid ""
"This server CANNOT encode AVIF - its image library was built without it, so "
"turning this on will produce no AVIF files. Ask your host for Imagick or GD "
"with AVIF support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:529
msgid "Stored Filenames"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:536
msgid "Hashed (recommended) — random 16-char filename, original kept as metadata"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:537
msgid "Original (sanitized) — keeps the user filename, capped at 100 chars"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:539
msgid ""
"How new uploads are named on disk. \"Hashed\" is more secure (no "
"enumeration) and avoids long-filename / emoji edge cases. Existing media is "
"never renamed."
msgstr ""

